WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.400
Okay. we have 21 hostages.

3
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.400
One child. Lina. daughter of Alex Maynard.
Soldier and head of this lab.

4
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.040
Her mother is in the Army.

5
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.000
She brought her to see her dad
when the situation began.

6
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.280
Lone terrorist.
Former lab staff. idealistic type.

7
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.880
He wants all of France to see
the weapons they're designing here.

8
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.280
He's unstable and paranoid.

9
00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:42.920
What goes on in that lab?

10
00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.200
We don't know. It's classified.

11
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.480
All I know is that it's explosives.

12
00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.080
Same partners as usual.

13
00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.480
Usual rules of engagement.

14
00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.600
Self-defense. hostage in danger.
or direct order.

15
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.880
The area is potentially explosive.

16
00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:01.320
Hold your fire.
We'll use the service corridors. Let's go!

17
00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.800
I want to speak
to the Minister of Defense.

18
00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.640
And I want a journalist.

19
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.080
Otherwise. I swear I'll kill someone.

20
00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.640
David. Laurent. in position.
Bravo Charlie.

21
00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.840
What do I have to do?

22
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.960
Shoot someone?

23
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:43.920
Is that it?

24
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.840
You have 15 minutes.

25
00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.880
Then I kill everyone. Do you hear me?

26
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.920
And don't try to buy time.

27
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.400
I know your tricks.

28
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.400
Okay. I have a visual on the hostages.

29
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.640
No visible injuries.

30
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.600
Do you understand?

31
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:02.680
Fuck!

32
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.760
Negotiations suspended.

33
00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.320
Fuck it!

34
00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.520
Visual on the target.

35
00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.760
He has a detonator in his left hand.

36
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.560
He looks agitated.
12-gauge pump-action shotgun.

37
00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.240
I've had enough.

38
00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.400
Don't look at me!

39
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.520
I've lost Oscar 13.

40
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.040
I don't see the girl. I can't find her.

41
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.360
Target is on the move.

42
00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.080
Shit!

43
00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:35.840
He's leaving the cafeteria.

44
00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.440
Watch out.
Oscar 9 is moving towards the back.

45
00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:41.760
I can't see her.

46
00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.320
She's taking a bag.

47
00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.960
What the fuck is she doing?

48
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.640
You.

49
00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:50.880
Get up.

50
00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.280
Now!

51
00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.120
Goddammit!

52
00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.840
She has a Beretta.
This is bad. Let's move fast.

53
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.360
Door may be rigged.
We'll go in through the back.

54
00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.000
You too! Get up!

55
00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.640
Get the fuck up. now!

56
00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.760
Fuck!

57
00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.000
Police!

58
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.240
-Police!
-It'll be okay. Listen to me.

59
00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.400
Target neutralized. One hostage hit.

60
00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.800
There! Secure the rear.

61
00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.720
-Look at me. honey.
-Sir. we need to evacuate.

62
00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.800
We need to apply pressure.
She's been shot.

63
00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.080
Follow me. Evacuate!

64
00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.440
We've got this. Come on.

65
00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.720
Come. We'll handle it.

66
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.280
-Get back. sir!
-She's been shot!

67
00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.520
There's a three-minute timer. Evacuate.

68
00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.680
Get back. sir!

69
00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:42.360
Ma'am. can you hear me? Can you hear me?

70
00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.880
-Keep going.
-Extraction!

71
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.240
Can you hear me?
Don't worry. we'll take care of you.

72
00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.040
My daughter…

73
00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.960
-Keep moving. Hurry.
-Did you hear me?

74
00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.320
I'm sure he set explosives.

75
00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.120
Where's your daughter?

76
00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.240
Go upstairs. sir. Please.

77
00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.160
Laboratory.

78
00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.080
In the lab?

79
00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.040
-He set explosives.
-We're on it.

80
00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:05.160
-My daughter is in the lab!
-Get him out!

81
00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.320
We're on it. Medic!

82
00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.320
-Doc! Over here!
-I'm a dad too. ma'am. I'm a dad too.

83
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.360
-I'll go get your daughter.
-My daughter…

84
00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:16.640
Come on. we're evacuating.
Go! Everybody. evacuate!

85
00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.360
No. wait! We need to find the girl!

86
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.080
She's missing. Christophe!

87
00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.520
You have 90 seconds.
then you need to get out.

88
00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.200
We didn't have much time.

89
00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.360
so Laurent and I
volunteered to go find the girl.

90
00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.280
We headed into the corridors and…

91
00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:48.320
Lina Mayard died
in the explosion that day.

92
00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:50.080
Like Lieutenant Villiers.

93
00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.240
Yeah.

94
00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.560
Fifteen years ago. tonight.

95
00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.720
Is there anything you remember.

96
00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.360
any detail you'd like to share with us?

97
00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.240
No.

98
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.720
Chloé. let's move on to his wife.

99
00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.480
This is Amal Mayard.

100
00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:10.360
She left the army and the country
after her daughter's death.

101
00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:11.760
She was declared dead.

102
00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:14.280
She committed suicide in Türkiye
one year later.

103
00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:16.440
Mayard. however. switched sides.

104
00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.480
He served ten years in Bois-d'Arcy prison
for arms trafficking.

105
00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:21.040
Including explosives back then.

106
00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.400
That's where he met Kröller.

107
00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:26.480
He got out last November.
No trace of him since.

108
00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:27.960
No digital trail. either.

109
00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:31.960
He used Kröller's network
to assemble the team that stole the CL20.

110
00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.880
We believe he's the one who killed Kröller
when we arrested him yesterday.

111
00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:37.480
He still has the 500 kilos.

112
00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.040
and he put some of it
in Christophe's ICU room.

113
00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:43.080
I put half of the Intel team on it.

114
00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:48.320
ELITE FORCE

115
00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:28.600
Not bad. right?

116
00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.960
Start your engine. Daktari. Let's listen.

117
00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.320
-Careful. guys.
-Listen up.

118
00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:35.720
Rev it up a bit.

119
00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:37.080
-Wait.
-Louder.

120
00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.040
-Louder?
-Yes.

121
00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:38.960
More?

122
00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.360
That noise is killing me. Stop!

123
00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:43.400
Speak up!

124
00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.600
-More?
-More!

125
00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:50.800
It's his foot!
Why don't you take your foot off?

126
00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.480
Laurent. I can make noise too.

127
00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:54.960
Okay. okay! Hands up!

128
00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:12.280
NATIONAL GENDARMERIE
GIGN

129
00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.520
COMMIT FOR LIFE

130
00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:16.000
So. how's the investigation going?

131
00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.280
They're making progress. but…

132
00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:27.520
All I wanted was
to be with him at the end.

133
00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:29.760
You got to be with him every day.

134
00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.720
They took him from me.

135
00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:38.000
They can't get away with this.

136
00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.080
They won't get away with it.

137
00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:44.680
I'll make sure of that.

138
00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.880
I've never seen that photo.

139
00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.200
We had a barbecue at Christophe's.

140
00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.840
You were there. actually.

141
00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.360
Yeah. I remember. I was ten. I think.

142
00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.640
Yeah.

143
00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:16.960
Do you know why you remember?

144
00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:18.480
No.

145
00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.240
Because you drank
an entire glass of wine that day.

146
00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:25.880
Yeah. I remember now.

147
00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.880
-My first alcoholic drink.
-Your mom caught us.

148
00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.880
My God. she really went off on us.

149
00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:33.960
Sorry.

150
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.600
I'm sorry about Christophe.

151
00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.280
As a kid. Dad would take me
to the Chinese buffet in Versailles.

152
00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.040
Just the two of us. It was our thing.

153
00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:57.120
Mom didn't like those kinds of places.

154
00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:02.120
I go every year.
on the anniversary of his death.

155
00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.400
Usually on my own. but…

156
00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:09.560
Since it's tonight. I thought maybe…

157
00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.880
Would you like to come with me?

158
00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:18.600
No.

159
00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.920
I never do anything. Ever.

160
00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.520
I need to go check something.

161
00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:31.720
Okay.

162
00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:47.280
IGGN breathing down our necks
won't speed things up.

163
00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:50.000
I might have a lead on Mayard.
Are you coming?

164
00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:36.760
MINISTRY OF JUSTICE
REPORT NUMBER 1

165
00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:38.720
Okay.

166
00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:44.920
FEBRUARY 10. 2011:
TRESPASSING AT A SECRET DEFENSE FACILITY

167
00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:49.160
VERSAILLES COURT
TWO YEARS IN PRISON

168
00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:01.520
David. I told you.
I'll call you as soon as I have something.

169
00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:03.040
Just checking. You never know.

170
00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.640
Well. I've got nothing. You can go now.

171
00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:17.080
Can I take a look?

172
00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:19.280
Sure.

173
00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:24.960
PROPERTIES

174
00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:29.040
LAST ACCESS:
TODAY. FEBRUARY 10. 2025. 2 MINUTES AGO

175
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:36.160
FEBRUARY 10. 2011:
TRESPASSING AT A SECRET DEFENSE FACILITY

176
00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:38.000
Where are you going?

177
00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.680
To the shooting range. You?

178
00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:45.920
Why are your guns in a bag?

179
00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:48.960
You're such a pain.

180
00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:51.640
What did you take? Can I see?

181
00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:05.440
Should I come with you?

182
00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:09.600
You're better off staying put.

183
00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.080
With that kind of gear.
it rarely ends well.

184
00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:21.240
Sometimes it's not meant to end well.

185
00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:08.320
SITUATION ANALYSIS
TARGET: VICTOR DUTEL - RETALIATION

186
00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:22.560
ONGOING OR PLANNED OPERATIONS
LT. DAVID BERGER. LT. LAURENT VILLIERS

187
00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:45.080
I followed because you said no.

188
00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:47.400
I figured out where you were going.

189
00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:51.040
We're 10 km from where Dad died.
on the day he died.

190
00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:57.120
Are you going
to pay your respects or something?

191
00:16:58.520 --> 00:16:59.640
Go home. Max.

192
00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:03.480
You know what?
I'm going to pay my respects. too.

193
00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:04.880
Don't worry. not with you.

194
00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:08.240
We'll go in separately. It's fine.

195
00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:16.200
You're right. I am going there.

196
00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.400
But it's not about Laurent.

197
00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:21.440
It's about Mayard.
the guy who killed Christophe.

198
00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:24.840
He lost his daughter in the explosion
that same day.

199
00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:27.360
He blames us for her death.

200
00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.880
I think he's doing all of this
to avenge her.

201
00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:33.960
Ten years ago. he was arrested
for trespassing on a military base.

202
00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:37.680
It was the same place.

203
00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.640
On the same date.

204
00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.520
Do you think he'll be there tonight?

205
00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.080
I don't know.

206
00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.400
You're arresting him alone?

207
00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:49.840
So you didn't get official orders. then?

208
00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:54.360
What are you doing?

209
00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:56.240
This is under the radar. I take it?

210
00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:57.840
No. it's not a mission.

211
00:17:57.920 --> 00:18:01.320
It's not under the radar.
It's nothing. Go home. Max.

212
00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.120
In that case. you're not in charge.

213
00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.400
That girl died at the same time as Dad.

214
00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:18.000
And you. my Dad's partner. my mentor.
were there. yet you want me out of this?

215
00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.120
Here.

216
00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:31.000
What's this?

217
00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:33.840
It's unlisted.

218
00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:36.080
Don't worry.

219
00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:45.680
We're only here to arrest Mayard. right?

220
00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:47.520
Obviously.

221
00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:03.840
It's a ten-minute walk.

222
00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:07.960
Remember how Dad liked riddles?

223
00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:10.760
Yeah.

224
00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:15.280
How do you flush out a terrorist
holed up with no hostages?

225
00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:19.560
Well. how do you do it?

226
00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:22.800
You wait for him to leave.

227
00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:34.480
You and your partner are unarmed.
A terrorist aims at you. What do you do?

228
00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.440
-Max.
-Do you know?

229
00:20:37.520 --> 00:20:39.400
Of course I do.

230
00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:42.600
You sacrifice yourself.

231
00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:44.520
You die for them.

232
00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:48.280
You don't die for them.

233
00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:50.560
You trust your partner.

234
00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.840
You put your life in their hands.
as they put theirs in yours.

235
00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:59.120
You count on them reacting when you act.

236
00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:03.040
The terrorist can't cover
two fronts at once.

237
00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:05.520
So you need total trust.

238
00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:08.720
Yeah.

239
00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:13.080
You must be sure that no matter what.
you're there for each other.

240
00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:18.600
Was it like that with you and Dad?

241
00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:23.200
That was a long time ago.

242
00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:52.720
On your back. Look out. Come on.

243
00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:53.640
Faster.

244
00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:56.240
Come on. keep your hips up.
Fill your lungs.

245
00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:57.400
Major.

246
00:22:00.240 --> 00:22:01.520
-Go on.
-Major.

247
00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:03.560
I'm kind of busy here.

248
00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:06.360
Where's Commander Berger?
I need to talk to him.

249
00:22:06.440 --> 00:22:08.640
I don't know. He's probably training.

250
00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:10.480
Where is he training?

251
00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:12.200
That's it. PJ. Good job.

252
00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:15.040
Major. it's important. It's about Mayard.

253
00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:18.960
Victor. can you take over?

254
00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:32.920
I don't know. Diving. jumping.
shooting. boxing. tech drills.

255
00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:35.480
We train 24/7. He could be anywhere.
I'm not his mom.

256
00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:37.720
I thought a section leader
trained with his men.

257
00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:43.800
Yeah. but today it's the anniversary
of his partner's death. so…

258
00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:46.920
He does what he has to do.
and I leave him alone. okay?

259
00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:48.840
Excuse me. I have a section to run.

260
00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:52.320
Come on. PJ. keep it up.
Do one more lap.

261
00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:55.120
That's it. fill your lungs…

262
00:23:23.320 --> 00:23:24.760
Is this the lab entrance?

263
00:23:25.600 --> 00:23:26.680
Yeah.

264
00:23:41.760 --> 00:23:42.600
Go.

265
00:23:45.280 --> 00:23:47.080
This is David. leave a message.

266
00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:05.120
DIED IN THE LINE OF DUTY
02.10.2010

267
00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:06.680
February 10.

268
00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:15.480
Shit. February 10.

269
00:24:15.560 --> 00:24:16.720
TRESPASSING
02.10.2011

270
00:24:24.840 --> 00:24:27.280
Get your team ready.
I think I found Mayard.

271
00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:29.640
I think Commander Berger is on his trail.

272
00:25:20.120 --> 00:25:21.560
This is where it happened?

273
00:25:25.480 --> 00:25:26.400
Yeah.

274
00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:09.800
What really happened here?

275
00:26:11.120 --> 00:26:12.240
What do you mean?

276
00:26:14.520 --> 00:26:19.080
Max. your father. Laurent. died.
and we all have to live with it.

277
00:26:19.160 --> 00:26:21.200
-That's what happened.
-That's bullshit.

278
00:26:22.400 --> 00:26:24.200
I read the after-action report.

279
00:26:24.280 --> 00:26:27.800
You were the only one with him.
Why's your report the only one missing?

280
00:26:27.880 --> 00:26:29.480
Why didn't Christophe say anything?

281
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.600
If there's nothing to hide.
where's the report?

282
00:26:34.000 --> 00:26:36.680
I was at rock bottom.
Can you understand that?

283
00:26:37.200 --> 00:26:39.760
Laurent was my best friend.
He was a brother to me.

284
00:26:40.840 --> 00:26:44.080
Police academy. pre-selection. training.
We did it all together.

285
00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:46.880
I was his best man.
I even became his son's mentor.

286
00:26:49.320 --> 00:26:52.040
I didn't write a report
because I wasn't able to.

287
00:26:53.480 --> 00:26:54.360
Satisfied?

288
00:26:56.040 --> 00:26:58.240
I was in the parking lot
on graduation night.

289
00:27:00.240 --> 00:27:02.760
Christophe asked you
if I knew the truth about Dad.

290
00:27:11.960 --> 00:27:13.320
What truth is that. David?

291
00:27:58.440 --> 00:27:59.280
Clear.

292
00:28:17.440 --> 00:28:18.600
Police! Stop!

293
00:28:26.320 --> 00:28:27.560
I'll go left.

294
00:28:52.720 --> 00:28:53.800
Max!

295
00:28:55.520 --> 00:28:56.520
Max!

296
00:29:00.360 --> 00:29:01.680
Max!

297
00:30:09.640 --> 00:30:11.600
-Are you okay?
-Yeah. he went that way.

298
00:31:07.720 --> 00:31:09.000
Max!

299
00:31:15.520 --> 00:31:16.680
Open your mouth.

300
00:31:39.560 --> 00:31:40.520
In the vest?

301
00:31:41.760 --> 00:31:42.800
Yeah.

302
00:31:48.400 --> 00:31:49.640
Shit.

303
00:32:02.720 --> 00:32:04.520
I struggle to remember her face.

304
00:32:05.040 --> 00:32:06.840
You know. my daughter.

305
00:32:07.600 --> 00:32:10.160
This is the only place
I can still picture her.

306
00:32:10.240 --> 00:32:12.400
I get to see her again. but only just.

307
00:32:14.880 --> 00:32:16.720
How are things with your partner?

308
00:32:22.920 --> 00:32:24.120
We tried to save her.

309
00:32:24.200 --> 00:32:26.120
No. you stopped me from saving her.

310
00:32:26.200 --> 00:32:27.440
I could have done it.

311
00:32:31.560 --> 00:32:33.360
Can you imagine losing a child?

312
00:32:33.440 --> 00:32:35.520
-I could've taken more from you.
-You okay?

313
00:32:36.320 --> 00:32:37.240
Yeah.

314
00:33:01.240 --> 00:33:03.080
Your father was a hero.

315
00:33:03.160 --> 00:33:05.280
He really tried to save my daughter

316
00:33:05.360 --> 00:33:07.800
-He gave his life for her.
-Shut up.

317
00:33:13.000 --> 00:33:14.040
On your knees.

318
00:33:18.880 --> 00:33:20.200
Legs crossed behind you.

319
00:33:24.960 --> 00:33:26.480
Hands on your head.

320
00:33:38.320 --> 00:33:39.160
Max.

321
00:33:39.920 --> 00:33:41.240
Will you watch him?

322
00:33:57.920 --> 00:33:59.400
That guy right there

323
00:33:59.480 --> 00:34:00.880
is a coward.

324
00:34:01.680 --> 00:34:04.240
Ever wonder why he made it out
and not your father?

325
00:34:10.200 --> 00:34:12.160
Ever heard of blast-proof armored doors?

326
00:34:13.160 --> 00:34:14.000
Shut it.

327
00:34:14.600 --> 00:34:16.440
No. apparently. you don't know.

328
00:34:17.960 --> 00:34:21.280
They were activated before the explosion.
From the inside.

329
00:34:22.480 --> 00:34:25.240
Only one person made it out. Him.

330
00:34:26.480 --> 00:34:28.920
Unfortunately.
there's only one explanation.

331
00:34:30.080 --> 00:34:33.120
He fled. sealing the blast doors
to save his own ass.

332
00:34:34.160 --> 00:34:39.000
He locked in my daughter and your father.
leaving them to die to save himself.

333
00:34:54.320 --> 00:34:57.480
Max!

334
00:35:32.040 --> 00:35:34.520
Look at me. Max. Listen to me.

335
00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:36.360
I'm the one who shot him.

336
00:35:36.880 --> 00:35:37.920
Okay?

337
00:35:38.000 --> 00:35:39.800
Is that clear? I shot him.

338
00:35:39.880 --> 00:35:41.560
And I was alone.

339
00:35:41.640 --> 00:35:42.600
Okay?

340
00:35:43.720 --> 00:35:44.560
Is it true?

341
00:35:46.120 --> 00:35:47.440
Is it your fault he died?

342
00:35:48.640 --> 00:35:51.640
You don't know what's at stake.
They're on their way.

343
00:35:51.720 --> 00:35:55.400
This is unauthorized. If they find out
you were here and you shot him.

344
00:35:56.800 --> 00:35:58.400
your GIGN career is over.

345
00:35:58.480 --> 00:36:02.560
I don't give a shit about my career!
I want to know what the fuck you did!

346
00:36:02.640 --> 00:36:06.240
Stop acting like a child!
Stop it right now!

347
00:36:06.320 --> 00:36:07.920
This is not the time to argue!

348
00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:12.120
You'll do exactly what I say.
Keep your phone turned off.

349
00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:14.000
Go back to your car.

350
00:36:14.080 --> 00:36:15.080
And go home!

351
00:36:15.160 --> 00:36:18.440
Don't say a word to anyone.

352
00:36:18.520 --> 00:36:19.640
Is that clear?

353
00:36:23.720 --> 00:36:25.800
And you do that right now.

354
00:36:26.600 --> 00:36:27.840
Get out of here!

355
00:42:12.680 --> 00:42:17.680
Subtitle translation by: Alison Simpson

355
